{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792503317,"nonce":"L8dwRFwG0I5ODaAq0g6q0Tn9qDU=","message":"Initial controls before the implementation: both new producer CPU tests failed with child alpha 0.25 instead of 0.5. Both offscreen application tests failed: static foreground overlap [64,128,64,255] instead of isolated [0,128,127,255], and foreground-only dynamic dispatch returned untouched blue. Logs: /private/tmp/blinc-fg-negative-cpu.log and /private/tmp/blinc-fg-negative-gpu.log.\n\nForeground commands now use a separate vector with foreground-local primitive/path cursors, owned by the active static/dynamic batch and saved through Pop. Only groups represented in the same batch and foreground stream are excluded from child alpha. Background ancestors and separately dispatched foreground RGBA retain their effective-opacity fallback. Foreground projection keeps its original aux rows; canvas foreground streams move into separate ordered batches. Static compositor baking omits foreground shapes and replays them once after canvas. Direct and both public glass hand-offs share the foreground dispatcher. Primitive-only cache mutations bail for foreground content or commands, including an empty zero-opacity group.\n\nExpanded tests caught two endpoint issues during implementation: settling at zero could erase the foreground group and let a later frame reuse an empty cache; and the compositor direct-write drift check compared translation but omitted opacity. Foreground opacity bindings now retain the group at endpoints and bypass the zero-opacity early return in their own foreground pass. The compositor compares cached binding opacity too, triggering the existing repaint fallback. Public glass fixture initially lacked TEXTURE_BINDING usage on its backdrop; that was a fixture validation error, corrected before pixel checks.\n\nAn earlier motion fixture placed a foreground element inside a background Motion wrapper. Its opaque-to-half frame remained opaque. That spans independent background/foreground streams and is outside this child scope. The final endpoint fixture puts the Motion wrapper inside a foreground ancestor, so the bound group is self-contained in the foreground stream. No cross-stream fix is claimed. Parent e0a7502 remains open for that case and separate text/SVG/ImageElement/RGBA streams, mixed CSS patching and named Sample.","files":null}]}